    - rid: 7112529932488278208
      type: {class: StickyNoteModel, ns: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework, asm: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework}
      data:
        Position: {x: 984.81744, y: -830.14844}
        ID:
          m_Value0: 16212589145827853325
          m_Value1: 4181618678885026579
        Parents: []
        PortModels: []
        Text: 'CHEAT SHEET FOR ABORT MODE CHOICE


          - Set to BOTH -


          IsDead


          IsStunned


          IsKnockedDown


          HasTarget
          (only if losing target should instantly exit combat)


          - Set
          to LOWER PRIORITY -


          InRange + CanAttack (punch/swing/slam/fire)


          PlayerTooClose
          / TooFar (movement choices)


          GrappleWindowOpen (if it should
          pre-empt lower behaviors)


          - Set to NONE (or SELF only) -


          Directional
          checks (front/behind) unless smoothed


          Random/utility conditions


          Anything
          that flickers a lot'
    - rid: 7112529932599951389
      type: {class: StickyNoteModel, ns: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework, asm: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework}
      data:
        Position: {x: -1443.247, y: 161.92772}
        ID:
          m_Value0: 13048873179877883896
          m_Value1: 1251317059931827678
        Parents: []
        PortModels: []
        Text: "NOTE: If \u201CDie branch\u201D is one action \u2192 no Sequence needed.\nIf
          \u201CDie branch\u201D is several actions in order \u2192 put a Sequence
          as the child of the guard, not above it.\n\nExample:\nGuard(IsDead) \u2192
          Sequence(StopMove \u2192 Die \u2192 Log)"
